          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 3,
          "question": {
            "text": "A mixture of chlorides of copper, cadmium, chromium, iron and aluminium was dissolved in water acidified with $\\mathrm{HCl}$ and hydrogen sulphide gas was passed for sufficient time. It was filtered, boiled and a few drops of nitric acid were added while boiling. To this solution ammonium chloride and sodium hydroxide were added and filtered. The filterate shall give test for.",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "4wi5i",
              "text": "Sodium and iron",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "CZuZP",
              "text": "Sodium and aluminium",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "rhhnP",
              "text": "Aluminium and iron",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "ahisu",
              "text": "Sodium, iron, cadmium and Al",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "CuS and CdS are precipitated by $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}$. Hydroxide of Al will pass into the solution in the form of $\\mathrm{NaAlO}_{2}$ being amphoteric in nature. Hence filtrate will give test for sodium and aluminium.",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
