          "question": {
            "text": "An aqueous solution of a substance gives a white precipitate on treatment with dil. HCl which dissolves on heating. When $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}$ is passed through the hot acidic solution, a black precipitate is obtained. The substance is a",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "IfzkF",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{Hg}_{2}^{2+}$ salt",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "AAAG8",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}$ salt",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "G73Kc",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{Ag}^{+}$ salt",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "YWYgG",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{Pb}^{2+}$ salt",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "$\\mathrm{PbCl}_{2}$ is insoluble in cold water, soluble in hot water and $\\mathrm{PbS}$ is black ppt in acidic medium.",
            "image": null
