        {
          "_id": "64c0e7fa6f5bfc7ab78ae984",
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "61a8bf0fc821b6514e527d7c",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2018-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2018",
              "title": "BITSAT 2018"
            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 3,
          "question": {
            "text": "When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> gas is passed into a mixture of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Hg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ion in an acidified aqueous solution, the precipitates formed are",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "D8z0e",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CuS</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HgS</mi></math>",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "CVF8b",
              "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MnS</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CuS</mi></math></p>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2luY1",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MnS</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NiS</mi></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "qLRmW",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NiS</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HgS</mi></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<p>In presence of acidic medium, ionisation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> is supressed so less number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> ions are produced. So only those sulphides are precipitated which have low solubility product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi>sp</mi></msub></mfenced></math> value.</p><p>Thus, in acidic medium, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> is very feebly ionised giving very small concentration of sulphide ion for precipitation. Therefore, the most insoluble salts <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CuS</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HgS</mi></math> are precipitated.</p>",
            "image": null
          },
